course: dictionary
lesson: 13875
title: Old words and drug safety
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Kief is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say some kief, not two kiefs. It has two meanings, and the context tells you which one is being used. The first meaning is a powder made from tiny hairs on the flowers of the cannabis plant, which is a drug and is illegal in many countries.
explain: The second meaning is old. In some old writing from North Africa and the Middle East, kief means a dreamy, lazy, peaceful feeling, as if you are half asleep. You will mostly meet this sense in old travel books, not in news reports.
explain: Look at the clues around the word: «The police said kief is an illegal drug, so no one should ever touch it.» The word illegal tells you it is against the law. Drug safety lessons teach that cannabis can harm a young person's growing brain, so if someone offers you kief, say no and tell a trusted adult.
fact: Kief is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some kief, not kiefs.
fact: Other spellings of kief are kif and kef.
fact: «Kief» means a powder made from tiny hairs on the cannabis plant, which is an illegal drug in many countries.
fact: In old writing, «kief» can mean a dreamy, lazy, peaceful feeling, as if half asleep.
fact: Cannabis can harm a young person's growing brain, so it is illegal for children everywhere.
exercise: «The police said kief is an illegal drug, so no one should ever touch it.» What is kief in this sentence? | *A powder made from cannabis plants, which is an illegal drug | A lazy cat that sleeps all day | A sweet cake sold in old markets | A type of warm tent
exercise: Drug safety lessons teach that cannabis can harm a young person's growing brain. Why is kief not for children? | It makes you grow taller very quickly | *It is illegal for children and can harm a growing brain | It is too cheap to be worth buying | It is only a flavour for cakes
exercise: «In an old travel book, the writer sank into a lazy kief in the cool shade.» What does kief mean here? | A loud argument with a friend | A sudden rush of hunger | *A dreamy, peaceful feeling, as if half asleep | A hard test at school
test: «The travellers rested in the shade and felt a sweet kief drift over them.» Which feeling does kief describe here? | Angry and loud | *Dreamy and peaceful, as if half asleep | Very hungry and rushing about | Wide awake and full of energy
test: Kief is an illegal drug in many countries. What is the safest choice if someone offers you some? | Keep it in your bag for later | Share it with your friends | Try a little to be brave | *Say no and tell a trusted adult
exam: Which statement about kief is true? | It is a type of bread eaten in old travel books | *It is a drug from the cannabis plant and is illegal in many countries | It is a legal sweet from the market | It is a kind of cloud seen at sunset
